      "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZWhpbWUtbnAuY28uanAvYXJ0aWNsZS9uZXdzMjAyNjEwMjMwMjI4",
      "headline": "県内の女性　はしか感染　松山市の施設で不特定多数と接触した可能性",
      "headlineTranslated": "Measles infection in a woman in the prefecture; possible contact with an unspecified number of people at a facility in Matsuyama City.",
      "summary": "Measles infection has been confirmed in a woman in her 50s in Ehime Prefecture, with possible exposure to an unspecified number of people at two Matsuyama City facilities during the infectious period. As of Oct 23, this is the prefecture's third confirmed measles case this year. Two exposure sites: Sogo Mart Uemoto Store (Kita-Uemoto-cho) in Matsuyama City, on Oct 19 from 5:00–5:20 pm; and Supermarket Nitto Kume Store (Minami-Kume-cho) on Oct 21 from 9:05–9:15 am. The article notes airborne measles virus can survive less than two hours. The woman had visited the same location as a man in his 30s confirmed infected in Matsuyama City on Oct 10. Measles is highly contagious, and infection can occur in those without immunity after exposure. The health department is advising customers who may have visited the sites during those times to monitor for symptoms and seek guidance.",
